{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/pulls/978","id":4218585267,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSbOoU877coCz","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/978","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/978.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/978.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/978","number":978,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(ci): stop CI/CD timeouts from hiding as cancelled runs","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #977.\n\n## The mechanism behind the whole issue\n\n> **A job killed by `timeout-minutes` is reported by GitHub as `cancelled`, not `failure`.**\n\nA run whose only non-success job is `cancelled` inherits the run conclusion `cancelled`, which on the runs list looks exactly like \"a human pressed cancel\" or \"a newer push superseded this run\". Grey, not red. No failure notification, no entry in the failed-runs filter.\n\nThat is why issue #977 describes the pipeline as `cancelled` rather than `failing`. The pipeline *was* broken — it just never said so.\n\n**18 consecutive `CI/CD Pipeline` runs on `main`** concluded `cancelled` between 2026-08-03T18:09 and 2026-08-06T05:13. The visible damage: the newest GitHub Release was **v0.326.1**, while crates.io already served **0.333.0** and git carried tags for eleven versions in between. **Eleven versions were tagged and published with no GitHub Release at all**, and CI stayed grey through all of it.\n\n## Root causes\n\n### RC1 — `Auto Release` hit its 30-minute cap (run `31065367736`)\n\n| Step | Window |\n| --- | --- |\n| `cargo build --release` | 02:53:54 → 03:02:08 |\n| publish to crates.io (0.333.0) | → 03:04:52 |\n| clean-install smoke test | 03:04:53 → 03:13:01 |\n| free runner disk | → 03:14:16 |\n| `docker buildx build --push` | 03:14:21 → **killed 03:22:04**, still at \"Compiling fs2 v0.4.3\" |\n\nThe PR-check `docker-build` job had used the GHA layer cache all along. The four **release** build-push steps had **no cache at all**, so every release recompiled the whole crate inside Docker — twice with Docker Hub enabled. `Create GitHub Release` sits after the Docker push and was never reached.\n\n### RC2 — `E2E Tests (local web app)` hit its 15-minute cap (run `31073507682`)\n\n`npx playwright install --with-deps chromium` ran **10 min 36 s**. Every library Chromium needs was already *\"the newest version\"*; the entire time went to apt fetching **font** packages from `azure.archive.ubuntu.com` at ~30–60 KB/s. That left ~4 minutes for `Running 468 tests using 2 workers`; the job died at test 159/468.\n\n**Compounding defect:** `globalTimeout` was `15 * 60_000` — *exactly* the job cap, which also pays for checkout, `bun install`, the bundle build, `npm ci` and the browser install. The job clock always won, so Playwright never aborted, never exited non-zero, `if: failure()` never fired, and **no report artifact was uploaded** — the one artifact that would have explained the run did not exist.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Errors**\n- GHA layer cache (`cache-from`/`cache-to: type=gha`) on **all four** release build-push steps.\n- `auto-release` / `manual-release`: `timeout-minutes` 30 → 60.\n- `--with-deps` split into an `actions/cache`-backed browser install plus a **bounded, non-fatal** `install-deps` step — in **both** `test-e2e-local` and `test-e2e-pages`. Headless Chromium runs without those fonts, so a slow mirror can no longer end the job.\n- `test-e2e-local`: `timeout-minutes` 15 → 40; `workers: 4` under CI (one per vCPU; these specs are I/O-bound).\n\n**False negatives**\n- `globalTimeout` 15 → 25 min, now well below the 40-minute job cap, so *Playwright* aborts first, exits non-zero, and leaves a report.\n- New terminal **`pipeline-status`** job (`scripts/check-pipeline-status.sh`) that `needs:` **every** other job and runs `if: always()`. Any `failure` is fatal; any `cancelled` is fatal **on `main`** — where `cancel-in-progress` is disabled, so a cancellation can only be a timeout or a manual cancel — and a `::warning::` elsewhere, where a supersede is legitimate.\n\n**Warnings**\n- Every action off the deprecated Node 20 runtime: `upload-artifact@v4→v7`, `download-artifact@v4→v8`, `setup-node@v4→v6`, `setup-python@v5→v6`, `checkout@v4→v6`, across all workflows.\n- `release.yml` was flagged as approaching its 2000-line ceiling. It is now **1948 lines — below its 1960-line starting point** despite gaining a job: six inline `run:` blocks became scripts, two of which (`configure-dockerhub-publishing.sh`, `invoke-create-github-release.sh`) were *byte-identical duplicates* across `auto-release` and `manual-release`.\n\n## Reproducing test\n\n`tests/unit/ci-cd/issue_977.rs` — **all ten assertions fail against the pre-fix tree and pass after** (verified by restoring the original `release.yml` and `playwright.local.config.js` and re-running). It covers: no `--with-deps` in any workflow, browser cache + bounded non-fatal apt step in both e2e jobs, `globalTimeout` < job cap, all four Docker steps cached, release budgets, the gate job's `needs:` covering every job (this caught a job I had missed), the deprecated-action sweep, and the shared-script extraction.\n\n`gate_script_behaves_correctly_for_every_conclusion` runs the gate script for real across success/skipped, cancelled-on-main, cancelled-off-main and failure. `experiments/issue-977-pipeline-status.sh` is the same four cases as a standalone script.\n\nExisting tests in `workflow_release.rs` and `issue_717.rs` were updated to follow the extracted logic into the scripts rather than dropped.\n\n## Evidence and analysis\n\n`dev/log/issues/977/pulls/978/` — both full run logs (25 609 and 31 816 lines) with per-step timings, run/annotation dumps, and **`ANALYSIS.md`** with the timeline, per-requirement root cause, prior art considered (`re-actors/alls-green`, `technote-space/workflow-conclusion-action`) and why a 20-line script fits better.\n\n## Upstream reports\n\nThe same defects exist in the pipeline templates, so they are filed there with reproducible examples, workarounds and code fixes:\n\n- link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template#118, link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template#123, link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template#50 — timeout-reported-as-cancelled (all three templates; verified none has an aggregate gate).\n- link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template#119 — uncached release Docker builds. **Verified as rust-only**: the js and python templates have a single, already-cached build step, so this was not reported against them.\n\nTemplate job-set diff: the rust template has `cargo-lock`, `coverage`, `deploy-docs` and `fresh-merge` as separate jobs. formal-ai already covers all four — fresh-merge via `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh`, Cargo.lock verification in `lint`, and coverage in its own `coverage.yml` (split out under #895 for the same line-limit reason).\n\n## Local verification\n\n`cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, `shellcheck --severity=warning` over all 18 tracked scripts, `rust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs`, and `cargo test --test unit ci_cd` (**172 passed, 0 failed**) all clean.\n\n## Not addressed, deliberately\n\n- **Recovering the 11 missing GitHub Releases** (v0.326.2 … v0.333.0). The tags and crates.io versions exist; backfilling the Releases is a one-off `gh release create` sweep over historical tags, not a pipeline change, and it rewrites public release history — worth doing, but as its own decision rather than folded into this PR.\n- **~25 source files in the 900–1000-line warning band** (`src/main.rs`, `src/solver.rs`, `tests/source/calculation.rs`, …). These are long-standing, predate this issue, and are only warnings; splitting them would be a large, risky refactor unrelated to the CI/CD failures. `scripts/check-file-size.rs` only reports warnings for files that *grew*, so they do not fire on unrelated PRs.\n","created_at":"2026-08-06T06:49:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T08:51:54Z","closed_at":"2026-08-06T08:51:52Z","merged_at":"2026-08-06T08:51:52Z","merge_commit_sha":"0a3fdc5649985f307c6ef4fab1b50b660d273691","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kona